                "dc.date.enforcement_date" : [ {
                  "value" : "24th July, 2020.-- S. 2 clauses (4), (13), (14), (16), (40), s. 10 to 27 (both inclusive), sub-clause (iv) of clause (a) of sub-section (1) of section 58, s. 88, 89, 92 and 93, 94, 96, 97 and 99, clause (f) to (m) of sub-section 2 and clauses (zg), (zh) and (zi) of sub-section 2 of s. 101, 104, vide notification No. S.O. 2421(E), dated 23rd July 2020, see Gazette of India, Extraordinary, Part II, sec. 3(ii).",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.date.entry_date" : [ {
                  "value" : "2020-08-03",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.date.issued" : [ {
                  "value" : "2019-08-09",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.description.abstract" : [ {
                  "value" : "The Consumer Protection Act, 2019\nStructure Highlights\n•\tChapters: At least IV (Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission) and mentions of other chapters (I - Preliminary, II - Consumer Protection Councils, III - Central Consumer Protection Authority)\n•\tSections: Snippets provided up to Section 93 (with gaps) and a separate snippet starting from Section 17\nKey Aspects Summarized by Category\n1. Consumer Protection Councils\n•\tCentral Consumer Protection Council: Established by the Central Government.\n•\tState Consumer Protection Councils: Established by State Governments.\n•\tDistrict Consumer Protection Council: Established by State Governments for each district.\n2. Central Consumer Protection Authority\n•\tEstablishment: Under Section 10, with a Chief Commissioner and Commissioners.\n•\tPowers & Functions: Protect consumer rights, prevent unfair trade practices, regulate false/misleading advertisements, and more.\n3. Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission\n•\tDistrict Forum: Handles complaints up to ₹20 lakhs with a President and two members.\n•\tComposition & Procedure: Detailed eligibility and procedural guidelines.\n4. Offences and Penalties\n•\tPenalties: For non-compliance, false advertisements, and adulterated/spurious goods, with varying imprisonment and fines.\n5. Complaint Mechanism\n•\tFiling Complaints: Electronically or in writing with the District Collector, Commissioner, or Central Authority.\nGaps in Summary\n•\tFull Structure: Missing due to snippet context.\n•\tDetailed Provisions: Many sections not included.\n•\tTransition & Miscellaneous: Not covered.",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.identifier.act_id" : [ {
